    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d450-a4">

                <pb facs="0619" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg523"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No.
                    21.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Minister for Foreign
                            Affairs to Mr. Tyler.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="hijri gregorian"
                            when="1898-04-20"><hi rendition="#italic">Zeekadeh 27, 1315</hi> (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 20, 1898.</hi>)</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    letter relating to the coming of Bagdasarian to Tabriz. It seems that the object
                    you had in view was to prevent his coming, but as it happened he arrived at that
                    city before the foreign office had taken measures to prevent it. Now it would
                    seem better to wait before making other representations until after the
                    examination has taken place.</p>
                <p>Receive the assurance, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mahmoor.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
